IsaacLab Arena CLI parser.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --variant {base,human,property,robot}
  --output OUTPUT
  --max-steps MAX_STEPS
  --handle-offset-y HANDLE_OFFSET_Y
  --handle-offset-z HANDLE_OFFSET_Z
  --variant-config VARIANT_CONFIG
  --adaptive-handle-height
  --validated-pregrasp
  --pregrasp-shortcut-policy {none,bounded_chords_v1}
  --pregrasp-settle-steps PREGRASP_SETTLE_STEPS
                        Hold the same planned pregrasp endpoint with bounded
                        increments before approach; inherited by matched
                        variants
  --planner-hazard-extra-padding-m PLANNER_HAZARD_EXTRA_PADDING_M
                        Additional conservative cuRobo hazard-box padding,
                        same matched policy; independent thresholds unchanged
  --task-id TASK_ID
  --grasp-roll-deg GRASP_ROLL_DEG
  --grasp-pitch-deg GRASP_PITCH_DEG
  --handle-normal-offset HANDLE_NORMAL_OFFSET
  --pull-lead-rad PULL_LEAD_RAD
  --pull-steps PULL_STEPS
  --ik-limit-margin-rad IK_LIMIT_MARGIN_RAD
                        Contract only local command IK bounds; source robot
                        limits remain unchanged
  --release-retreat-m RELEASE_RETREAT_M
                        Checked outward TCP retreat during finger release;
                        same policy for baseline and variants
  --release-tilt-deg RELEASE_TILT_DEG
                        Tilt outward release direction toward world up;
                        negative moves down, same matched policy
  --opening-reserve-rad OPENING_RESERVE_RAD
                        Additional measured opening before release; native
                        predicate and all collision checks stay active
  --release-retreat-profile {linear,ease_out}
                        Same bounded retreat endpoint; optional early progress
                        with a slower finish, inherited by matched variants
  --release-command-policy {full_pose,bounded_position_v1,bounded_position_hold_v2}
  --release-settle-steps RELEASE_SETTLE_STEPS
                        Additional closed-gripper hold at one measured joint
                        target before release; inherited by matched variants
  --mode {collect,neutral}
  --render-warmup       Converge RTX appearance with no physics advancement
                        before recording
  --neutral-seconds NEUTRAL_SECONDS
  --review-config REVIEW_CONFIG

app_launcher arguments:
  Arguments for the AppLauncher. For more details, please check the
  documentation.

  --livestream {0,1,2}  Force enable livestreaming. Mapping corresponds to
                        that for the `LIVESTREAM` environment variable.
  --xr                  Enable XR mode for VR/AR applications.
  --device DEVICE       The device to run the simulation on. Can be "cpu",
                        "cuda", "cuda:N", where N is the device ID
  --visualizer VISUALIZER, --viz VISUALIZER
                        Visualizer backends to enable as CSV (e.g.,
                        kit,newton,rerun,viser).
  --verbose             Enable verbose-level log output from the
                        SimulationApp.
  --info                Enable info-level log output from the SimulationApp.
  --experience EXPERIENCE
                        The experience file to load when launching the
                        SimulationApp. If an empty string is provided, the
                        experience file is determined from the resolved
                        visualizer and XR settings. If a relative path is
                        provided, it is resolved relative to the `apps` folder
                        in Isaac Sim and Isaac Lab (in that order).
  --deterministic       Request reproducible rendering (see AppLauncher docs).
  --kit_args KIT_ARGS   Command line arguments for Omniverse Kit as a string
                        separated by a space delimiter. Example usage:
                        --kit_args "--ext-folder=/path/to/ext1 --ext-
                        folder=/path/to/ext2". A single Kit argument works in
                        both forms: --kit_args "--ext-folder=/path/to/ext1" or
                        --kit_args=--ext-folder=/path/to/ext1.
  --anim_recording_enabled
                        Enable recording time-sampled USD animations from
                        IsaacLab PhysX simulations.
  --anim_recording_start_time ANIM_RECORDING_START_TIME
                        Set time that animation recording begins playing. If
                        not set, the recording will start from the beginning.
  --anim_recording_stop_time ANIM_RECORDING_STOP_TIME
                        Set time that animation recording stops playing. If
                        the process is shutdown before the stop time is
                        exceeded, then the animation is not recorded.
  --max_visible_envs MAX_VISIBLE_ENVS
                        When set, caps the nums of envs shown in the launched
                        visualizers.

Isaac Lab Arguments:
  Arguments specific to Isaac Lab framework

  --disable_fabric      Disable fabric and use USD I/O operations.
  --seed SEED           Optional seed for the random number generator.
  --num_envs NUM_ENVS   Number of environments to simulate.
  --env_spacing ENV_SPACING
                        Spacing between environments.
  --mimic               Enable mimic environment.
  --distributed         Run distributed (one process per GPU). Use with
                        torchrun; AppLauncher uses LOCAL_RANK for device.

Isaac Lab Arena Arguments:
  Arguments specific to Isaac Lab Arena framework

  --enable_cameras      Add the environment's camera sensors and observations.
  --no_solve_relations  Disable solving spatial relations in the environment.
  --placement_seed PLACEMENT_SEED
                        Seed for live solved object placement. Ignored when
                        recorded placement is replayed.
  --presets {physx,newton}
                        Arena physics backend preset: 'physx' or 'newton'.
                        When not set, each environment uses its own default.
  --resolve_on_reset, --no-resolve_on_reset
                        Re-place objects from the pool on each reset (default:
                        True). Use --no-resolve_on_reset to keep the same
                        layout.
  --list_variations     Print Hydra-configurable variations for the selected
                        environment and exit.

External Environments Arguments:
  Arguments specific to external environments

  --external_environment_class_path EXTERNAL_ENVIRONMENT_CLASS_PATH
                        Name of the external environment to run

Environment Graph Spec Arguments:
  Arguments specific to environment graph spec

  --env_spec ENV_SPEC   Path to an environment graph spec YAML. When set, the
                        environment is built from the graph spec instead of a
                        registered example-environment name; the env-name
                        subcommand then becomes optional. Any override flags
                        the YAML declares under `cli_override_specs` are added
                        to the parser dynamically.
